---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import BattleGrid from '../components/BattleGrid.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';

const baseUrl = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout title="Game Systems & Battle Tactics" description="Comprehensive guide to Radiant Historia combat mechanics, 3x3 grid positioning, turn swapping, Mana Bursts, and time-travel rules.">
  <div class="container intro-container">
    <Breadcrumbs
      items={[
        { label: 'Compendium Hub', href: baseUrl },
        { label: 'Systems & Battle Tactics' }
      ]}
    />

    <header class="page-header glass-card">
      <div class="header-badge">Core Gameplay &amp; Strategy</div>
      <h1 class="page-title">Game Systems &amp; Battle Mechanics</h1>
      <p class="page-subtitle">
        Everything you need to master *Radiant Historia*: 3×3 grid maneuvers, turn swapping, combo stacking, Mana Bursts, and the temporal laws of The White Chronicle.
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Author Preface -->
    <section class="glass-card section-card">
      <div class="card-header">
        <span class="card-icon">📜</span>
        <h2 class="card-title">Author's Preface &amp; Guide Philosophy</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="prose-content">
        <p>
          <em>Radiant Historia</em> is one of the most uniquely engaging RPGs of its era, featuring unforgettable music by Yoko Shimomura, an intricate geopolitical plot, and a brilliant tactical turn-based combat system.
        </p>
        <p>
          This walkthrough is designed to provide information organized as cleanly and efficiently as possible:
        </p>
        <ul class="styled-list">
          <li><strong>Zero Level Grinding:</strong> The recommended levels in this guide are calibrated for fighting natural random encounters without tedious grinding.</li>
          <li><strong>Zero Item/Gold Farming:</strong> No reliance on low-percentage rare drops. Boss steal targets are guaranteed steals when using Stocke or Aht.</li>
          <li><strong>Zero Missables Policy:</strong> Every single hidden chest, sidequest trigger window, node requirement, and shop inventory update is documented.</li>
        </ul>

        <Callout type="note" title="Plot Spoilers Notice">
          Walkthrough chapters are written to avoid major narrative spoilers while giving clear tactical directions. However, the <strong>236 Node Completion List</strong> contains historical outcomes and ending summaries, so review it with caution if playing for the first time.
        </Callout>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 3x3 Grid Battle Tactics -->
    <section class="glass-card section-card">
      <div class="card-header">
        <span class="card-icon">📐</span>
        <h2 class="card-title">The 3×3 Tactical Battle Arena</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="prose-content">
        <p>
          Unlike standard turn-based RPGs, enemies in <em>Radiant Historia</em> occupy specific tiles on a <strong>3 rows × 3 columns grid</strong>. Understanding row distance is vital:
        </p>

        <div class="grid-rules-cards">
          <div class="rule-card rule-front">
            <h4 class="rule-title">Front Row</h4>
            <p>Enemies deal full physical damage but take <strong>+25% increased damage</strong> from all party attacks. Ideal target for early elimination.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rule-card rule-center">
            <h4 class="rule-title">Center Row</h4>
            <p>Standard baseline damage dealt and received. Most human and medium-sized enemies spawn here.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rule-card rule-back">
            <h4 class="rule-title">Back Row</h4>
            <p>Enemies take <strong>~40% reduced physical damage</strong> but deal less physical damage. Mages and ranged archers frequently position here.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h3>Positioning Skills &amp; Stacking Enemies</h3>
        <p>
          The true power of the battle system lies in <strong>pushing multiple enemies into the exact same tile</strong>. When multiple foes occupy one tile, every subsequent attack hits <em>all of them simultaneously</em>!
        </p>

        <div class="table-responsive">
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Skill Name</th>
                <th>User</th>
                <th>Effect &amp; Grid Movement</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>Push Assault</strong></td>
                <td>Stocke, Raynie, Marco, Aht, Gafka, Eruca</td>
                <td>Knocks the target 1 row backward into the tile behind them.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>Left Assault</strong></td>
                <td>Stocke, Rosch</td>
                <td>Knocks the target 1 column to the left.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>Right Assault</strong></td>
                <td>Stocke</td>
                <td>Knocks the target 1 column to the right.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>Grapple (Pull)</strong></td>
                <td>Marco, Rosch</td>
                <td>Pulls the target 1 row forward into the frontline.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>Air Assault</strong></td>
                <td>Stocke, Aht, Gafka</td>
                <td>Launches the enemy into the air, keeping them vulnerable for aerial juggling combos.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><strong>Bedrock Smash</strong></td>
                <td>Gafka</td>
                <td>Gafka’s signature heavy impact: drags all surrounding enemies into the center tile.</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Embedded Battle Grid -->
      <BattleGrid interactive={true} />
    </section>

    <!-- Turn Manipulation & Trans-Turn -->
    <section class="glass-card section-card">
      <div class="card-header">
        <span class="card-icon">⚡</span>
        <h2 class="card-title">Turn Manipulation &amp; The Trans-Turn System</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="prose-content">
        <p>
          At the top of the combat screen, the upcoming turn order is displayed as a queue of character/enemy portraits. You can <strong>Change (Swap) Turns</strong> at any time:
        </p>

        <ul class="styled-list">
          <li><strong>Turn Swapping:</strong> You can swap a party member's turn with any upcoming ally or enemy turn.</li>
          <li><strong>Vulnerability Penalty:</strong> Swapping turns makes that character turn red (Vulnerable), causing them to take critical damage if attacked before their turn arrives.</li>
          <li><strong>Consecutive Party Combos:</strong> By grouping all party turns together consecutively, you can execute unbroken 6-to-12 hit combo strings without enemy interruption.</li>
          <li><strong>Trans-Turn Skill:</strong> Marco and Eruca learn <em>Trans-turn</em> (3 MP), which instantly transfers their active action to another ally without incurring the Vulnerability penalty!</li>
        </ul>

        <Callout type="warning" title="Boss Turn Swapping Strategy">
          Against deadly bosses (like Palomides or Hugo), use turn swaps to align 6 party turns in a row. Have Stocke push the boss onto Aht’s elemental traps, follow up with Marco’s Trans-turn, and unleash Raynie's high-tier magic for over 2,000+ damage!
        </Callout>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- The White Chronicle Rules -->
    <section class="glass-card section-card">
      <div class="card-header">
        <span class="card-icon">✨</span>
        <h2 class="card-title">The White Chronicle &amp; Temporal Paradoxes</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="prose-content">
        <p>
          The White Chronicle allows Stocke to record pivotal historical events as <strong>Historia Nodes</strong>. Through Teo and Lippti at the realm of Historia, you can travel freely back to any visited node with your current levels, equipment, and abilities intact.
        </p>

        <div class="grid-rules-cards">
          <div class="rule-card">
            <h4 class="rule-title">Cross-Timeline Causality</h4>
            <p>Obstacles in Standard History often require finding knowledge, skills, or items in Alternate History, and vice-versa.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rule-card">
            <h4 class="rule-title">Possible Histories (Bad Endings)</h4>
            <p>Wrong choices lead to tragic historical conclusions. Experiencing a Bad Ending does not cause a Game Over; it simply unlocks a special White Chronicle node and returns you to the decision point.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="rule-card">
            <h4 class="rule-title">Sidequest Progression</h4>
            <p>Many sidequests span across multiple chapters and parallel timelines. Completing all sidequests is mandatory for the true grand ending.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .intro-container {
    padding-bottom: 4rem;
  }

  .page-header {
    border-top: 3px solid var(--gold-primary);
    padding: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.5rem);
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .header-badge {
    font-family: var(--font-ui);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--gold-primary);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .page-title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .page-subtitle {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    max-width: 850px;
  }

  .section-card {
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  .card-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    padding-bottom: 0.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .card-icon {
    font-size: 1.4rem;
  }

  .card-title {
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    color: var(--gold-primary);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .prose-content {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .prose-content p {
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }

  .prose-content h3 {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    color: var(--text-bright);
    margin: 1.75rem 0 0.85rem 0;
  }

  .styled-list {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin: 1rem 0 1.5rem 0;
    padding-left: 0.5rem;
  }

  .styled-list li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
  }

  .styled-list li::before {
    content: '◆';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--gold-primary);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    top: 0.2rem;
  }

  .grid-rules-cards {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
  }

  .rule-card {
    background: rgba(6, 9, 15, 0.6);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    padding: 1.2rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .rule-front { border-top: 3px solid #ef4444; }
  .rule-center { border-top: 3px solid #eab308; }
  .rule-back { border-top: 3px solid #38bdf8; }

  .rule-title {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    color: var(--text-bright);
  }

  .rule-card p {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
</style>
